# Documentation discipline

Before exploring or grepping broadly, read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [INDEX.md](../../INDEX.md).

## When editing a folder

1. Read that folder's `INDEX.md` first.
2. If you add/remove/rename a significant file, update the folder `INDEX.md`.
3. Match existing table style and "one concern" tone.

## When adding an API route

1. Add file-header comment (purpose, auth, rate limit, schema).
2. Update [app/api/INDEX.md](../../app/api/INDEX.md).
3. Update [docs/API.md](../../docs/API.md).

## When adding a page route

1. Update [app/INDEX.md](../../app/INDEX.md).
2. Add file-header on `src/page-components/*Page.tsx`.

## When adding customer-visible behavior

Update [docs/help/](../../docs/help/INDEX.md) in plain language — no internal file paths.

## When adding a lib domain (>5 files)

Create `src/lib/{domain}/` + `INDEX.md` (model: `src/lib/coach/`).

## Do not

- Use `~/.cursor/plans/` as source of truth — use `PLAN.md` / `LOG.md`.
- Open deleted paths listed in INDEX.md §4.
- Add docs under `src/locales/` — deprecated.

## Hub

[docs/README.md](../../docs/README.md) — all audiences.
